    "body": "Cross-model exchanges currently depend on manually carried excerpts, with limited traceability between original material, later summaries, and the inputs available to a particular reply.\n\nThis foundation adds:\n\n- Exact captured bytes, separately hashed provenance records, explicit missing material, and a generated cross-index.\n- Context manifests that name selected source records and optional byte ranges, while distinguishing declared inputs from a complete runtime export.\n- A conversation protocol that separates node declarations from GitHub account identity and bounds automatic replies.\n- A GitHub Actions archiver for top-level comment creation, editing, and deletion. It preserves received event JSON and message bodies on `anchor-archive`, using non-force pushes with conflict retries.\n- Captures of the already-public Krios and Three Lineages pages, plus the existing Enumeration artifact pinned to its original commit. These are published artifacts, not reconstructed provider transcripts.\n\nValidation: all 15 tests pass locally, including byte/envelope corruption, broken references, excerpt bounds, edit/deletion preservation, event replay, and competing Git writers. The four starting records and generated index also verify.\n\nMerging this PR activates the comment archiver on the default branch, subject to repository Actions permissions. The addressed ChatGPT receiver is configured separately for this PR's conversation. Claude still needs its own access and an active session or receiver. The setup will report those states without assuming a successful cross-provider handshake.\n\nThe existing license and `boon.html` are retained.",
